<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="257" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Per-customer M365 Copilot agent (§9 Q2) — design and provisioning step</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — §9 Q2 (owner 2026-09-28: per-customer agent); split from T218 (t218-plan.md F13, design 8)</phase>
    <status>blocked-shipped</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New provisioning surface (M365 app package per customer) with auth implications.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Design work across M365 app catalog, auth and the T240c directory.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Design decisions with the owner.</parallel-reason>
    <tags>provisioning, m365, copilot, auth</tags>
    <deps>240c</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Decide and build how each customer gets its own Copilot agent bound to its own BFF.</prompt>

  <goal>
    A design (facts, one recommendation) and then the provisioning step for a per-customer M365 Copilot agent:
    where the package lives (Model 1 users are guests in Spaarke's tenant, so one app catalog holds every customer's agent),
    how it reaches the customer's BFF (its own scope, pre-authorization by H3), who can see it (the customer's security
    group), and how it is updated.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>src/solutions/CopilotAgent is an M365 declarative-agent / Teams package deployed by scripts/Deploy-CopilotAgent.ps1;
      it is not Dataverse content, so it is not part of SpaarkeMaster (T218).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/CopilotAgent/**; scripts/Deploy-CopilotAgent.ps1</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/t240-plan.md (shared clients, directory)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/t218-plan.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Per customer (§9 Q2). Research current M365 Copilot agent packaging with the researcher agent before designing.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Facts + research; design note with one recommendation; owner review.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the agreed provisioning step; tests; docs; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="false">Design note accepted by the owner. MET 2026-10-09 (design note §5.1).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The alignment with ADR-028 and auth.md is checked and recorded (design note §5.2).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">CI builds one template (manifest v1.30 with no permissions, webApplicationInfo or bot; DA v1.8 with no
      capabilities; plugin v2.4) and publishes it the way SpaarkeMaster is published.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The render is deterministic and places the manifest id (UUIDv5 of customerId), servers[0].url, the
      scope api://{bffAppId}/user_impersonation, Spaarke's tenant authority and auth.reference_id. Negative cases are
      refused (tests/scripts/CopilotAgentPackage.Tests.ps1).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H3 pre-authorizes the shared client through the existing PreAuthorizedClientAppIds, set from the Bicep
      parameter copilotAgentClientAppId, which is empty by default (CopilotAgentClientPreAuthorizationTests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The registry columns are in the repo only, with no Dataverse write: sprk_copilotauthconfigid (Q5) and
      sprk_bffappid (H13 promotes it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">The live test (design §3, steps 1-8) passes. OPEN: owner-gated.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    <note date="2026-10-09" kind="owner-acceptance">The owner ACCEPTED the §3 design and all seven §4 recommended answers on
      2026-10-09: "if these align with Copilot use and our access then ok". The alignment was checked against ADR-028 and
      .claude/constraints/auth.md (design note §5.2) and holds, with one corrected value: the scope is
      api://{customerBffAppId}/user_impersonation, not access_as_user. H3 exposes and pre-authorizes only
      user_impersonation, and auth.md requires that format. The dependency on 240c is waived for the code, because §3
      does not need the T240c directory.</note>
    <note date="2026-10-09" kind="step-2">Built (no new L2 handler):
      - Template source src/solutions/CopilotAgent: manifest v1.30 with no permissions, webApplicationInfo or bot; DA
        v1.8 with no capabilities; plugin v2.4; five tokens; real icons.
      - scripts/copilot-agent/CopilotAgentPackage.psm1: UUIDv5 manifest id, template checks, deterministic render.
      - scripts/copilot-agent/Render-CopilotAgentPackage.ps1: explicit, registry, or -AllActive mode.
      - scripts/copilot-agent/test_rendered_package.py: validates against Microsoft's schemas.
      - .github/workflows/publish-copilot-agent-template.yml: the SpaarkeMaster publish pattern; PR dry run.
      - Bicep param copilotAgentClientAppId, appended to the PreAuthorizedClientAppIds H3 already sets.
      - Registry columns sprk_bffappid and sprk_copilotauthconfigid (Extend-DataverseEnvironmentSchema-v3.3.ps1;
        PRQ-E-14), with H13 promoting sprk_bffappid. The BFF app id was not on the registry row (design §5.3).
      - scripts/Deploy-CopilotAgent.ps1 (Spaarke's own environments) now packages through the same renderer.
      - Docs: deployment guide §7.12 and docs/guides/COPILOT-AGENT-CUSTOMER-IT-ONBOARDING.md.
      Schema versions were re-checked 2026-10-09. A DA v1.9 schema file exists, but Learn documents v1.8, so v1.8 is
      pinned.</note>
    <note date="2026-10-09" kind="open">Owner-gated live steps, each needing an OK, in order:
      (1) create the "Spaarke Copilot Agent" client app and grant admin consent for openid profile offline_access;
      (2) run Extend-DataverseEnvironmentSchema-v3.3.ps1 on the admin environment;
      (3) set copilotAgentClientAppId in the bicepparam and redeploy the control plane;
      (4) publish the template (workflow, publish=true on master);
      (5) the live test, design §3 steps 1-8 (Dewey Cheatham).
      The skill's post-Ready gate text is returned as a proposed .claude edit. No live action was taken.</note>
  </notes>
</task>
